# CSS Components Usage Guide

This guide explains how to **use** the available CSS components in the design system.  
All components follow the **BEM (Block Element Modifier)** naming convention and use the `ft-` prefix.

Each component is designed to provide consistent, theme-based styling that can be extended or customized via CSS variables — not by modifying core classes.

---

## List Component (`ft-list`)

The **`ft-list`** component is used to display structured lists with optional headers and interactive items.  
It supports buttons, links, and general clickable or static elements.

### Basic Structure

The `ft-list` component provides a flexible layout for displaying grouped items, optionally with headers.

```html
<div class="ft-list">
  <div class="ft-list__header">Section Header</div>

  <button class="ft-list__item">Item 1</button>
  <button class="ft-list__item ft-active">Item 2 (Active)</button>
  <a href="#" class="ft-list__item">Item 3 (Link)</a>
</div>
```

### Main Elements

Each `ft-list` is composed of a container (`.ft-list`) and its internal elements, which follow the BEM naming convention for clarity and consistency.

| Element | Selector | Description |
|----------|-----------|--------------|
| **List Container** | `.ft-list` | The main wrapper that defines the layout and behavior of the list. It controls padding, width, and background inheritance. |
| **Header** | `.ft-list__header` | Represents the section header of the list. It typically contains a label, title, or icon. Aligns content horizontally with `display: flex` and maintains a minimum height of `3rem`. |
| **Item** | `.ft-list__item` | Defines a list element that can represent a link, button, or static row. It inherits text color and font size from the theme variables and spans the full width of the container. |

#### Example

```html
<div class="ft-list">
  <div class="ft-list__header ft-d-f ft-g-3">
    <ft-icon name="folder"></ft-icon>
    Documents
  </div>

  <button class="ft-list__item">Reports</button>
  <a href="#" class="ft-list__item">Invoices</a>
  <button class="ft-list__item ft-active">Receipts</button>
</div>
```

### Notes

- **Semantic Flexibility:**  
  The `.ft-list__item` element can be used with semantic tags such as `<div>`, `<button>`, or `<a>`.  
  Choose the tag based on the intended interaction:
  - `<button>` for in-app actions.
  - `<a>` for navigation.
  - `<div>` for static or non-interactive items.

- **Active and Hover States:**  
  Interactive list items automatically display hover and active states:
  - Hover state applies `background-color: var(--ft-list-item-hover-bg)`.
  - Active state uses `.ft-active` to apply `background-color: var(--ft-list-item-active-bg)`.

- **Header Behavior:**  
  Headers can overlap or stick based on modifiers:
  - `.ft-overlapped` allows visual overlap with content below by adjusting the clipping area.
  - `.ft-list--sticky-header` keeps headers fixed at the top of the list during scroll.

- **Spacing and Typography:**  
  The list uses theme variables such as:
  - `var(--ft-text-font-size-md)` for consistent text size.
  - `var(--ft-text-color)` for unified text color across themes.

- **Accessibility:**  
  Ensure interactive items have proper ARIA roles and keyboard focus states when using `<div>` elements for interactivity.
